# About 10 Projects

Bounded pieces of work with a goal and a status. Each project is one note (`type: project`) and usually its own folder, so the plans, logs, captures and drafts it generates have somewhere to live alongside it — that supporting material is `type: working`, project state rather than knowledge. A project note says what the work is, where it stands, and what it touches; it links to the knowledge, sources, decisions and outputs involved instead of holding copies of them. When a project ends, what it *taught* you moves to `20 Knowledge/` and the folder itself moves to `90 Archive/`.
